1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:03,276
Sim's memory windowing has unit tests.

2
00:00:03,276 --> 00:00:09,086
But if a change broke how the final request is put together, those tests would not show it.

3
00:00:09,086 --> 00:00:11,129
This harness makes that visible.

4
00:00:11,629 --> 00:00:18,162
It replays one hundred twenty made-up conversations through Sim's real windowing code, unchanged.

5
00:00:18,162 --> 00:00:20,249
Plain code checks each request.

6
00:00:20,249 --> 00:00:21,259
No model judge.

7
00:00:21,759 --> 00:00:22,700
Four settings.

8
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:25,791
With no memory, every fact is lost, by design.

9
00:00:25,791 --> 00:00:30,898
Full context keeps seventy nine percent on dev and eighty seven on held out.

10
00:00:30,898 --> 00:00:34,526
The ten message window keeps fifty four and sixty two.

11
00:00:34,526 --> 00:00:37,549
The token window, fifty eight and sixty five.

12
00:00:38,049 --> 00:00:39,186
Here is one case.

13
00:00:39,186 --> 00:00:42,530
An order ID is given, then eleven messages follow.

14
00:00:42,530 --> 00:00:45,741
Full context and the token window still hold it.

15
00:00:45,741 --> 00:00:48,549
The ten message window has already cut it.

16
00:00:49,049 --> 00:00:51,431
Bulky tool results change the picture.

17
00:00:51,431 --> 00:01:00,329
Only three messages follow the fact here, yet the four thousand token window lost it, because one tool result is bigger than the whole window.

18
00:01:00,829 --> 00:01:04,755
To trust the checker, I broke request assembly seven ways.

19
00:01:04,755 --> 00:01:05,703
It caught six.

20
00:01:05,703 --> 00:01:10,170
The one it missed is a real gap in my cases, and the page says so.

21
00:01:10,670 --> 00:01:16,335
What is faked: token counts, model limits, and there is no live model or summary mode.

22
00:01:16,335 --> 00:01:19,630
Facts kept means the exact text is in the request.

23
00:01:20,129 --> 00:01:23,789
The next step would be running the same check on real traces.

24
00:01:23,789 --> 00:01:26,789
This is a harness, not a claim that Sim has a bug.
